From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:34:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms, nvidia-drm: report failed HDMI FRL link training of a
 modeset

When FRL link training fails in a modeset, nvHdmiFrlSetConfig() fakes it to
keep the display engine from hanging and logs a warning. The display stays
black and no client finds out. It also retries right away, while amdgpu waits
200 ms before a retry.

Wait 200 ms between the retries. After a failure reassess the link and send a
dpy event. nvidia-drm then sets the connector's link-status to BAD before its
hotplug event, as the DRM docs describe for this case, so the compositor sets a
mode again, using the rates that still work. Stop reporting after 3 failures in
a row, so that a link that keeps failing doesn't cause modesets forever. A
successful training or probing the display again resets the count.

The state reaches nvidia-drm through a new read-only dpy attribute, added at
the end of the enum, so the NVKMS ABI of userspace clients doesn't change.

The wait holds nvkms_lock, for up to 1 s more on a modeset that fails.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
